\subsection{Parameter Sensitivity Analysis}
\subsubsection{Hidden Dimension $d_{\text{model}}$}
We analyze the sensitivity of Paloma to the hidden dimension $d_{\text{model}}$, as shown in Figure~\ref{fig:hyper_para_d_model}. 
% Overall, Paloma exhibits stable performance across a wide range of $d_{\text{model}}$ values. 
As $d_{\text{model}}$ increases from small to moderate values, the performance consistently improves, indicating that a larger representation capacity helps capture richer temporal patterns. 
However, when $d_{\text{model}}$ becomes sufficiently large, the performance tends to saturate, with only marginal gains or slight fluctuations observed.
Notably, this trend is consistent across all datasets, indicating that while performance improves with increasing $d_{\text{model}}$ at smaller scales, it becomes stable beyond a moderate range. 
This suggests that Paloma is not highly sensitive to the choice of $d_{\text{model}}$ once sufficient model capacity is reached, and can achieve strong performance without requiring excessively large dimensions. 


